Add an explicit user-assigned XZ composite profile for controlled XR1710G
6 GHz tests.

XR1710G exposes all three bands through one shared PHY, so cfg80211 applies a
single regulatory domain to 2.4, 5 and 6 GHz. XZ therefore carries the pinned
AU 2.4/5 GHz rules together with the isolated 6 GHz 36 dBm laboratory rule.
XZ is not an ISO country domain and this is not an AFC implementation. Keep
the ordinary US and AU rules unchanged. The UI labels this profile as an
opt-in composite laboratory profile. Selecting XZ does not grant Standard
Power authorization. Operators remain responsible for local authorization
and compliance.
---
--- a/db.txt
+++ b/db.txt
@@ -2201,3 +2201,24 @@ country ZW: DFS-ETSI
 	(5250 - 5330 @ 80), (20), DFS, AUTO-BW
 	(5490 - 5710 @ 160), (27), DFS
+
+# XR1710G controlled laboratory composite profile. All XR1710G radios share
+# one PHY and therefore one cfg80211 regulatory domain. Keep the pinned AU
+# 2.4/5 GHz rules here so those bands remain available while the owner opts
+# into the 6 GHz laboratory rule. XZ is a user-assigned code, not a country
+# regulatory domain. This profile has no AFC implementation and does not
+# represent Standard Power authorization. Never select it automatically.
+country XZ: DFS-ETSI
+	# AU Item 3 and 7: 2.4 GHz
+	(2400 - 2483.5 @ 40), (4000 mW)
+
+	# AU Items 10, 11, 12(a), 12(b), 9 and 22: 5 GHz
+	(5150 - 5250 @ 80), (200 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, AUTO-BW
+	(5250 - 5350 @ 80), (100 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, AUTO-BW, DFS
+	(5470 - 5600 @ 80), (500 mW), DFS
+	(5650 - 5730 @ 80), (500 mW), DFS
+	(5730 - 5850 @ 80), (4000 mW), AUTO-BW
+	(5850 - 5875 @ 20), (25 mW), AUTO-BW
+
+	# XR1710G 6 GHz controlled laboratory rule; no AFC implementation.
+	(5925 - 7125 @ 320), (36), NO-OUTDOOR
